<title>NIGERIA: Nigerian oil products pipeline vandalised.</title>
<headline>Nigerian oil products pipeline vandalised.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Nigerian National Petroleum Corp (NNPC) said its pipeline supplying oil products to some parts of eastern Nigeria had been disrupted.</p>
<p>It said in a statement on Sunday that the break occured along kilometre 45 and 65 in the Isiala Ngwu council area.</p>
<p>&quot;This act of vandalisation was a result of the nefarious activities of some unscrupulous people,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>NNPC said despite the disruption it would ensure there was no scarcity of fuel products in the east during the Christmas festivities.</p>
<p>Criminals periodically hack into NNPC pipelines, sometimes with disastrous consequences, to steal oil.</p>
</text>
